{"title":"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_-_Combinations\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 - Combinations</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(HOW_TO_THINK_CRITICALLY!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CRITICALLY!!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the expression <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/8/30841790d6df05e01324bf04a96c40b291b8da30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\underline{\\qquad}\\times\\underline{\\qquad}\\right)+\\left(\\underline{\\qquad}\\times\\underline{\\qquad}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"226\" height=\"18\" /> each blank is to be filled in with one of the digits <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/1/1614f2a4d8d2f0e92b1b76f39417aacfbaba9e2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,2,3,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"47\" height=\"16\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/5/4054552638cf9f29e857a1306bd3ec31df3c19b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"15\" /> with each digit being used once. How many different values can be obtained?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/f/76facc6cd1c4d16c1234590efc60a2081426f903.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }2 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) }3\\qquad \\textbf{(C) }4 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) }6 \\qquad \\textbf{(E) }24 \\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"362\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_-_Combinations\">Solution 1 - Combinations</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 - Combinations\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/2/54216aeffa0fa278199cd3ceeb64cc8400c4a8cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{4}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"39\" height=\"55\" /> ways to choose the pairs(because once we choose 2 numbers to go in the first 2 slots the left 2 numbers fill in the other 2 slots), and we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/c/08ce4ccc8f0624befaa9ce7855fc1afc69b8e5ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2!$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> ways for the values to be rearranged, hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/0/f205d5b89072b705ba077c79d0140debb6053674.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{6}{2}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"94\" height=\"38\" />\n~minor edit Washingtonsee\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We have four available numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/f/6ff3584203afeaeba1a976ba69d5d362d20328af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 2, 3, 4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"18\" />. Because different permutations do not matter because they are all addition and multiplication, if we put <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> on the first space, it is obvious there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/a/4faa3b02b5b2deb20b9cae1911c4231bd3342042.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"55\" height=\"28\" /> possible outcomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/b/afb27f1814a41725b350272ae48ec33ad501a551.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2, 3, 4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"59\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/a/2da866442e69c040daf44260b4728d37e98de313.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4!$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> ways to arrange the numbers and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/5/2c5cc1e7f294a032ab77989acd0f30cbf9a011e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2!2!2!$\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" /> overcounts per way due to commutativity. Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/e/66eddf42261d26547857807c837078ce38c69b32.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4!}{2!2!2!}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"128\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>~MC_ADe\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/2/50257e1113399bb38a23519393448f182d5f410d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{3}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"33\" height=\"53\" /> ways to choose which two numbers will not be multiplied by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> (This step is useful since multiplying by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> won't a change the final outcome). Thus, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/3/633e43acc2ad546abdf9752e07ec489ae46d1a37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{3}{2}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"118\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p>~pandapower24\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28HOW_TO_THINK_CRITICALLY.21.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(HOW_TO_THINK_CRITICALLY!!!)\">Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CRITICALLY!!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CRITICALLY!!!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/clLyv4GFtto\">https://youtu.be/clLyv4GFtto</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/KpC9wT7HgBo\">https://youtu.be/KpC9wT7HgBo</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"